          "date": "2026-11-17 15:58:04.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-21164 obdclass: share the checksum dump code",
        "message": "LU-21164 obdclass: share the checksum dump code\n\nThe osc and the target each have a dump_all_bulk_pages() that writes\nthe pages of a bulk with a checksum error to a file. The two differ\nonly in the \"osc\" or \"ost\" part of the file name and in how the pages\nare mapped, so every change has to be made twice, most recently for\nscoped_with_init_fs().\n\nMove the common parts to obdclass as obd_cksum_dump_open(),\nobd_cksum_dump_write() and obd_cksum_dump_close(), and leave only the\nloop over the pages to the callers. Stop at the first write error\ninstead of trying each remaining page. Also fix the osc unmapping the\npage by the address it had advanced past the data written.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Id2c824ca40fb7cfcb87e9c042952d281d685a73a\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
